  "id": "COMPOUND:36680 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 10,17-Dioxosparteine interacts with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, through a series of target-mediated pathways involving Caspase-5. This compound appears to act as a target of multiple compounds, all of which are implicated in the regulation of the SDR family member 9. The evidence is consistent with a role for 10,17-Dioxosparteine in modulating the activity of Caspase-5, which is a key player in the extrinsic apoptotic pathway. The SDR family member 9 is known to be involved in the metabolism of various substrates, and its interaction with 10,17-Dioxosparteine may be mediated through a direct or indirect interaction with the enzyme. The presence of multiple distinct compounds that target Caspase-5 and ultimately SDR family member 9 suggests a potential mechanism involving the regulation of enzymatic activity or the modulation of downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism where 10,17-Dioxosparteine may influence the function of the SDR family member 9 through its interaction with Caspase-5, although further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
